    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute concerns the SGD 4.00 no-show cancellation fee on trip TRP-09101. The fee stands and the driver is compensated.\n\nThe charge is validated under POL-NS-01 on all four limbs. (a) The trip record contains a driver 'arrived' event at 08:10:20. (b) The GPS trace places the driver 24.01 m from the pickup pin, inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius, and the first in-geofence fix at 08:10:00 precedes the arrival marker. (c) The driver held position in-geofence for 320 continuous seconds, measured from the first qualifying fix at 08:10:00 to the last at 08:15:20, against the 300-second STANDARD minimum. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 08:15:20 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event.\n\nNone of the displacing clauses applies. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: at the arrival marker the driver was stationary at 0.0 km/h about 24 m from the pin, so the marker is neither remote (300 m) nor in motion (15 km/h). POL-NS-06 yields no shortfall: effective dwell 320 s exceeds the 300 s minimum, and the only advisory artifact, EV-ADVIS-09101-01, is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), so its accumulation limb is unavailable and could not be asserted for either party. POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it. POL-NS-04 does not apply: the chat log contains no rider locating or coordinating message, so limb (a) fails, and the platform's rider track places the rider's device 519.37 m from the pin with rider_qualifying_fix_count of 0 against the 100 m STANDARD radius, so limb (c) fails affirmatively. The rider's account that he was 'downstairs' is a statement, not a chat message, and the platform's own rider track contradicts it; it is noted but does not carry the rider's case.\n\nUnder POL-NS-07 the driver is owed 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee, that is SGD 3.20, the residual 20 percent being the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, and 1 against 120 completed trips in 30 days is well below 0.08. Per POL-GEN-03 the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd; the rider's own charge is unchanged rather than refunded.\n\nThe rider's request to escalate under POL-NS-09(a) is rejected. Confidence is capped by the artifacts carrying the deciding facts, and those are the GPS trace, trip record, chat log and fare breakdown, all at weight_multiplier 1.0; bundle_integrity_score is not the cap. No POL-NS-09 trigger engages: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, the counterparty-dispute counters are both 0, the anti-farming check does not trip and rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, and no POL-NS-08 limb is met so nothing is impaired or down-weighted. The rider's margin point does not create doubt: measured from the arrival marker the wait is exactly 300 seconds and measured from the first in-geofence fix it is 320, both at or above the minimum, on a trace with 100 percent coverage, 33 fixes and zero sampling gaps. POL-NS-08 is satisfied on every limb — arrival-marker skew is 20 seconds, the trace has no gap over 120 seconds and more than 6 fixes, the chat log has 3 messages matching trip_record.chat_message_count with sequential msg_ids, and the SGD 4.00 cancellation line equals the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00).\n\nOn the profiles: only the counters that POL-NS-07 and POL-NS-09 name were used; every other profile field is context only under POL-GEN-01 and none was relied on. The driver's counterparty statement and contemporaneous chat messages are consistent with the telemetry but POL-NS-03, the clause that reads them, does not arise here."
